ws" id=3D"news"></a>Life Sciences Digest - In the News</h2><h3 style=3D"font-=
family:Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif;font-size:17px;color:#12395b;margin:=
22px 0 8px;">Executive Summary</h3>
<ul style=3D"margin:0 0 12px;padding-left:22px;">
<li style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-hei=
ght:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 6px;">Elebsiran plus tobevibart drove hepati=
tis delta virus below detection in 79% of Phase 3 participants, establishing =
a credible U.S. filing path despite an unusually weak delayed-treatment compa=
rison. (<a href=3D"https://investors.vir.bio/news/news-details/2026/Vir-Biote=
chnology-Announces-Primary-Endpoint-Met-in-Pivotal-Phase-3-ECLIPSE-1-Trial-fo=
r-Elebsiran-and-Tobevibart-in-Chronic-Hepatitis-Delta/default.aspx" style=3D"=
color:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:underline;">Vir Biotechnology, <em>Vir Biotechn=
ology Announces Primary Endpoint Met in Pivotal Phase 3 ECLIPSE 1 Trial</em>,=
 November 8, 2026</a>)</li>
<li style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-hei=
ght:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 6px;">Edwards=E2=80=99 PROGRESS trial moves =
TAVR into selected moderate aortic stenosis, reducing death or heart-failure =
events by an absolute 7.2 percentage points without demonstrating a mortality=
 benefit. (<a href=3D"https://www.nejm.org/doi/full/10.1056/NEJMoa2607326" st=
yle=3D"color:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:underline;">New England Journal of Medic=
ine, <em>TAVR in Patients with Moderate Aortic Stenosis with At-Risk Features=
</em>, November 2, 2026</a>)</li>
<li style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-hei=
ght:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 6px;">Pelacarsen and ziltivekimab each chang=
ed its target biomarker substantially but produced hazard ratios near 1.00 fo=
r cardiovascular events, weakening two major prevention hypotheses.</li>
<li style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-hei=
ght:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 6px;">FDA simultaneously demonstrated flexib=
ility and caution toward AAV gene therapy by accepting AMT-130 on externally =
controlled data from 12 patients while confirming Zolgensma-related insertion=
al oncogenesis.</li>
<li style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-hei=
ght:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 6px;">CMS finalized a permanent negotiation =
framework that will group certain route-changing fixed combinations with thei=
r original products, reducing the economic value of formulation-based lifecyc=
le extensions beginning in 2029. (<a href=3D"https://www.cms.gov/newsroom/fac=
t-sheets/medicare-drug-price-negotiation-program-medicare-prescription-drug-b=
enefit-program-final-rule-cms" style=3D"color:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:underli=
ne;">CMS, <em>Medicare Drug Price Negotiation Program Final Rule</em>, Novemb=
er 5, 2026</a>)</li>
</ul>
<h3 style=3D"font-family:Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif;font-size:17px;col=
or:#12395b;margin:22px 0 8px;"><a id=3D"story-1" name=3D"story-1" style=3D"co=
lor:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:underline;"></a>1. Elebsiran plus tobevibart esta=
blishes a Phase 3 path toward deep hepatitis delta suppression</h3>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>What changed</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">In the 124-patient ECLIPSE 1 trial, mo=
nthly elebsiran plus tobevibart produced undetectable hepatitis delta virus R=
NA and normalized ALT in 44% of participants at week 48, versus 0% in the del=
ayed-treatment group at week 12. Seventy-nine percent achieved undetectable v=
irus, and all met the broader virologic-response definition. One grade 3 trea=
tment-related neutrophil decrease occurred, with no treatment discontinuation=
s. (<a href=3D"https://investors.vir.bio/news/news-details/2026/Vir-Biotechno=
logy-Announces-Primary-Endpoint-Met-in-Pivotal-Phase-3-ECLIPSE-1-Trial-for-El=
ebsiran-and-Tobevibart-in-Chronic-Hepatitis-Delta/default.aspx" style=3D"colo=
r:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:underline;">Vir Biotechnology, <em>Vir Biotechnolog=
y Announces Primary Endpoint Met in Pivotal Phase 3 ECLIPSE 1 Trial</em>, Nov=
ember 8, 2026</a>)</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>What it tells us</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">The result validates simultaneous supp=
ression of hepatitis B surface-antigen production with siRNA and viral entry =
or particle clearance with an antibody. Deep suppression across cirrhotic and=
 non-cirrhotic patients strengthens the regulatory case. The design compares =
different treatment durations rather than equal-time concurrent therapy, howe=
ver, and the endpoints remain virologic and biochemical rather than decompens=
ation, liver cancer or mortality.</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">Commercially, monthly administration c=
ould offer meaningful convenience. Global differentiation still depends on di=
rect performance against bulevirtide.</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>What to watch next</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">ECLIPSE 2 and the head-to-head ECLIPSE=
 3 results, durability after treatment withdrawal and the planned mid-2027 FD=
A submission.</p>
<hr style=3D"border:0;border-top:1px solid #d5dde3;margin:18px 0;"/>
<h3 style=3D"font-family:Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif;font-size:17px;col=
or:#12395b;margin:22px 0 8px;"><a id=3D"story-2" name=3D"story-2" style=3D"co=
lor:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:underline;"></a>2. Early TAVR reduces heart-failu=
re events in selected moderate aortic stenosis</h3>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>What changed</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">PROGRESS randomized 744 patients with =
moderate aortic stenosis and at least one symptom or structural risk feature =
to Edwards=E2=80=99 balloon-expandable TAVR or surveillance. At two years, de=
ath or a heart-failure event occurred in 16.7% versus 23.9%, an absolute diff=
erence of 7.2 percentage points. Heart-failure events fell from 19.0% to 10.8=
%, while mortality was 8.4% with TAVR and 7.3% with surveillance. More than h=
alf the surveillance group underwent valve replacement during follow-up. (<a =
href=3D"https://www.acc.org/Latest-in-Cardiology/Articles/2026/11/01/00/11/mo=
n-1240pm-progress-tct-2026" style=3D"color:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:underline;=
">American College of Cardiology, <em>PROGRESS: TAVR Superior to Clinical Sur=
veillance in Patients With Moderate AS</em>, November 2, 2026</a>; <a href=3D=
"https://www.nejm.org/doi/full/10.1056/NEJMoa2607326" style=3D"color:#1a5e9a;=
text-decoration:underline;">New England Journal of Medicine, <em>TAVR in Pati=
ents with Moderate Aortic Stenosis with At-Risk Features</em>, November 2, 20=
26</a>)</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>What it tells us</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">PROGRESS supports earlier intervention=
 for a selected, predominantly symptomatic population whose disease frequentl=
y progresses within two years. The benefit is morbidity reduction and improve=
d health status, not longer survival. That distinction matters when weighing =
procedural risk, valve durability and cost.</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">Commercial significance could be subst=
antial because moderate disease is outside the current U.S. indication. Edwar=
ds gains first-mover evidence, although broader category expansion would also=
 benefit competing TAVR manufacturers.</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>What to watch next</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">FDA label strategy, guideline changes,=
 reimbursement and whether longer follow-up shows durability or a mortality d=
ifference.</p>
<hr style=3D"border:0;border-top:1px solid #d5dde3;margin:18px 0;"/>
<h3 style=3D"font-family:Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif;font-size:17px;col=
or:#12395b;margin:22px 0 8px;"><a id=3D"story-3" name=3D"story-3" style=3D"co=
lor:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:underline;"></a>3. Pelacarsen and ziltivekimab sh=
ow that biomarker control does not establish cardiovascular benefit</h3>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>What changed</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">Detailed Lp(a)HORIZON results showed t=
hat pelacarsen lowered lipoprotein(a) by approximately 78%, yet cardiovascula=
r events occurred in 12.3% of treated patients and 12.1% of controls (hazard =
ratio 1.02). Even among patients with baseline Lp(a) of at least 90 mg/dL, ev=
ent rates were identical at 12.3% (hazard ratio 1.00). (<a href=3D"https://ww=
w.nejm.org/doi/full/10.1056/NEJMoa2610159" style=3D"color:#1a5e9a;text-decora=
tion:underline;">New England Journal of Medicine, <em>Pelacarsen and Cardiova=
scular Outcomes in Patients with High Lipoprotein(a)</em>, November 7, 2026</=
a>)</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">ZEUS produced the same disconnect: zil=
tivekimab inhibited interleukin-6 and lowered inflammatory markers but did no=
t reduce cardiovascular events in patients with atherosclerosis and chronic k=
idney disease (hazard ratio 0.99). (<a href=3D"https://www.nejm.org/doi/full/=
10.1056/NEJMoa2612126" style=3D"color:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:underline;">New=
 England Journal of Medicine, <em>Interleukin-6 Inhibition with Ziltivekimab =
for Atherosclerotic Disease</em>, November 7, 2026</a>)</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>What it tells us</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">The new data resolve whether obvious s=
ubgroups could rescue either program: none did. Pelacarsen=E2=80=99s failure =
weakens, without refuting, the broader Lp(a)-lowering thesis because competin=
g siRNAs may achieve different depth, duration or biology. ZEUS similarly tes=
ts one antibody in a severely ill population rather than disproving cardiovas=
cular inflammation as a target.</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">Both results raise the commercial evid=
entiary bar: biomarker magnitude cannot substitute for outcomes trials.</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>What to watch next</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">Event data for olpasiran and lepodisir=
an, and analyses explaining why genetic risk associations failed to translate=
 pharmacologically.</p>
<hr style=3D"border:0;border-top:1px solid #d5dde3;margin:18px 0;"/>
<h3 style=3D"font-family:Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif;font-size:17px;col=
or:#12395b;margin:22px 0 8px;"><a id=3D"story-4" name=3D"story-4" style=3D"co=
lor:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:underline;"></a>4. FDA advances AMT-130 as confir=
med Zolgensma insertional oncogenesis raises the AAV safety bar</h3>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>What changed</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">FDA accepted uniQure=E2=80=99s AMT-130=
 Huntington=E2=80=99s disease BLA for accelerated approval and set May 1, 202=
7 as the target decision date. The application relies on 36-month results fro=
m 12 high-dose patients compared with an external control. At 48 months, the =
12-patient cUHDRS analysis was not statistically significant, although total =
functional capacity favored treatment nominally; a randomized 200-patient con=
firmatory trial is planned. (<a href=3D"https://uniqure.gcs-web.com/news-rele=
ases/news-release-details/uniqure-announces-third-quarter-2026-financial-resu=
lts-and" style=3D"color:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:underline;">uniQure, <em>uniQ=
ure Announces Third Quarter 2026 Financial Results and Provides Company Updat=
e</em>, November 4, 2026</a>)</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">Separately, FDA confirmed two Zolgensm=
a tumor cases in which vector DNA integrated near or within the GLI1 oncogene=
. The agency extended the identified neoplasia risk to Itvisma, which uses th=
e same vector and construct, while maintaining that both products=E2=80=99 be=
nefits outweigh their risks. (<a href=3D"https://www.fda.gov/vaccines-blood-b=
iologics/safety-availability-biologics/fda-investigating-serious-risk-maligna=
ncy-linked-zolgensma-gene-therapy" style=3D"color:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:und=
erline;">FDA, <em>FDA Investigating Serious Risk of Malignancy Linked to Zolg=
ensma Gene Therapy</em>, November 6, 2026</a>)</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>What it tells us</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">BLA acceptance confirms regulatory wil=
lingness to consider sparse, externally controlled evidence in fatal neurodeg=
eneration; it does not resolve AMT-130=E2=80=99s efficacy uncertainty. The Zo=
lgensma findings convert insertional oncogenesis from a theoretical label ris=
k into a demonstrated product-related event. The appropriate read-through is =
stricter construct-specific integration analysis and long-term surveillance, =
rather than a class-wide conclusion about all AAV therapies.</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>What to watch next</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">A potential AMT-130 advisory committee=
, FDA action on Zolgensma labeling and tumor-monitoring requirements across r=
elated programs.</p>
<hr style=3D"border:0;border-top:1px solid #d5dde3;margin:18px 0;"/>
<h3 style=3D"font-family:Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif;font-size:17px;col=
or:#12395b;margin:22px 0 8px;"><a id=3D"story-5" name=3D"story-5" style=3D"co=
lor:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:underline;"></a>5. CMS closes a formulation route=
 around Medicare negotiation</h3>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>What changed</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">CMS finalized rules governing Medicare=
 drug-price negotiation for prices effective in 2029 and beyond. When product=
s from the same application holder share an active ingredient and an added co=
mponent creates a new formulation enabling another administration route, CMS =
will generally aggregate them as one qualifying single-source drug. CMS expli=
citly cited products combining an active ingredient with hyaluronidase as an =
example. The rule takes effect December 5, 2026. (<a href=3D"https://www.cms.=
gov/newsroom/fact-sheets/medicare-drug-price-negotiation-program-medicare-pre=
scription-drug-benefit-program-final-rule-cms" style=3D"color:#1a5e9a;text-de=
coration:underline;">CMS, <em>Medicare Drug Price Negotiation Program and Med=
icare Prescription Drug Benefit Program Final Rule</em>, November 5, 2026</a>=
)</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>What it tells us</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">The final rule reduces the ability to =
protect economics by shifting an established infused biologic into a subcutan=
eous fixed combination shortly before negotiation. Convenience, chair-time sa=
vings and improved adherence retain clinical and competitive value, but the n=
ew formulation may inherit the original product=E2=80=99s maximum fair price =
exposure.</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">The policy favors lifecycle strategies=
 that demonstrate additional clinical benefit, reach a distinct population or=
 introduce a genuinely new molecule. It also makes negotiation timing more im=
portant in decisions to license formulation technology or fund route-switchin=
g trials.</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>What to watch next</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">CMS=E2=80=99s February 1, 2027 selecti=
on of up to 20 Part B and Part D drugs for the 2029 cycle and manufacturers=
=E2=80=99 responses to the aggregation policy.</p>
